# Cypress tests in Fernly

## 1. Queries

Prefer Testing Library order: `findByRole`, then `findByLabelText`, then `findByText`. Never target CSS module classes or raw tag names.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — web/cypress/component/QuantityStepper.cy.tsx
cy.findByRole('button', { name: 'Increase quantity' }).click();

// ❌ BAD — class from QuantityStepper.module.css
cy.get('button.QuantityStepper-module__button').last().click();
```

## 2. States

Assert `disabled`, `checked`, or values on the DOM node. Chaining `.should()` onto `findByRole` makes failures look like “element not found” when the locator worked.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
cy.findByRole('button', { name: 'Increase quantity' }).then(($el) =>
  expect($el, 'Increase quantity at stock limit').to.be.disabled,
);

// ❌ BAD — same file today; misleading failure text
cy.findByRole('button', { name: 'Increase quantity' }).should('be.disabled');
```

## 3. Waiting

Never sleep for a fixed duration. Wait on an intercepted API alias or on what the customer sees.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — UI test on browse
cy.intercept('GET', '/api/plants*', { fixture: 'plants/browse-positive.json' }).as('plants');
cy.visit('/');
cy.wait('@plants');
cy.findByRole('heading', { name: /browse/i });

// ❌ BAD
cy.visit('/');
cy.wait(500);
```

## 4. Data

Component tests pass props in the mount. UI tests load responses from `web/cypress/fixtures/` — one file per scenario (positive, negative, edge).

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — component props in QuantityStepper.cy.tsx
cy.mount(<QuantityStepper value={3} max={3} onChange={cy.spy()} />);

// ✅ GOOD — fixture per scenario
cy.fixture('plants/catalog-error.json').then((body) => {
  cy.intercept('GET', '/api/plants*', { statusCode: 500, body }).as('plantsFail');
});

// ❌ BAD — huge inline catalog in the spec
cy.intercept('GET', '/api/plants*', { items: [/* 21 plants pasted here */] });
```

## 5. Mocks

Stub only Fernly API traffic under `/api/*`, with an alias. Never intercept the Vite app shell or static assets.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
cy.intercept('GET', '/api/plants*', { fixture: 'plants/browse-positive.json' }).as('plants');

// ❌ BAD
cy.intercept('GET', '**/*', { fixture: 'plants/browse-positive.json' });
cy.intercept('GET', '/', { body: '<html>fake</html>' });
```

## 6. Tags

Exactly one level tag per test: `{ tags: '@component' }` or `{ tags: '@ui' }`. A confirmed product bug adds `@known-bug` so CI can exclude it until fixed (`grepTags=-@known-bug`).

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
it('disables − at the minimum', { tags: '@component' }, () => { /* … */ });

// ❌ BAD — no tag, or tag only on describe
describe('QuantityStepper', { tags: '@component' }, () => {
  it('disables − at the minimum', () => { /* … */ });
});
```

## 7. App code

Do not change `web/src` to green a test. If the test matches `docs/PRODUCT.md`, record it in `FINDINGS.md` (see F-01).

```markdown
<!-- ✅ GOOD — FINDINGS.md evidence cites the failing spec -->
- **Evidence:** `web/cypress/component/QuantityStepper.cy.tsx`, test "disables + at the stock limit"

<!-- ❌ BAD — “fixing” QuantityStepper.tsx value > max to pass the test without product approval -->
```

## 8. Evidence

Label how each claim was verified: **executed** (test or command run), **inspected** (code or walk only), or **not yet tested**.

```markdown
<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
- **Evidence:** … fails under `npm run cy:component` (executed).

<!-- ✅ GOOD — FINDINGS.md suspicions -->
- **CareLevelBadge** — code: `LABELS[Math.min(level, 2) - 1]` (inspected, not yet tested).

<!-- ❌ BAD -->
- Quantity stepper probably broken (guess, no test or steps).
```
